{"id": "EUVD-2026-93306", "enisaUuid": "175d8fb8-b972-31be-8f2b-6f51460fd09b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nf_nat: unregister and release hooks on error\n\nIf nf_hook_entries_insert_raw() fails, the NAT hooks get never released,\nresulting in a memleak.\n\nPostpone setting nat_proto_net->nat_hook_ops when the hooks are\nregistered to simplify the error path to decide whether the nat hooks\nneed unwinding.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79084567cd082fb4482e1ea457580e7d6504dd99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df80342f4bfc023ad7d6703df5e27f583ff0cb8d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbdd39ce42530a193c56beb206a3356cb6d01016"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98321", "GHSA-4xqv-x9wj-55p5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06f280a2-8246-3429-81e6-2a2f3f858835", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "499c439f-8c90-3aad-a5a9-757b3ee2432a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1cd472bf036ca038e783ef5f058f54e45b7e8180 <df80342f4bfc023ad7d6703df5e27f583ff0cb8d"}, {"id": "49a6e6b7-58f8-34fc-9bd6-e6396df41dbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "b5e547d5-17c7-3418-a2ac-14d6be8edbba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1cd472bf036ca038e783ef5f058f54e45b7e8180 <79084567cd082fb4482e1ea457580e7d6504dd99"}, {"id": "c6040554-ca20-3f82-99f5-feaad9545bdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.18"}, {"id": "e22a8454-6eab-3c9d-b8c4-330e63a25ea4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1cd472bf036ca038e783ef5f058f54e45b7e8180 <cbdd39ce42530a193c56beb206a3356cb6d01016"}, {"id": "f03a510